{#
settings/_compose_behavior.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
How the compose window behaves for this user — whether a forward opens with
its quoted original folded behind the "show quoted text" pill, what a send
shows while it is held — and, last, whether this browser hands its mailto:
links to plMail at all.

A plain form that submits on change and redirects, exactly like the clock
beside it: the choice matters on the next compose window, not on this page,
so there is no fragment worth streaming back. The control is the two-segment
idiom every boolean on the appearance page wears.
#}
{% set segText = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                  peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                  peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                  transition-colors cursor-pointer' %}

{# The body inset, which this card never had.

   settings/_card.html.twig pads a body only when asked (`padded`), because
   most of them are lists that pad their own rows — and the three cards beside
   this one on the General page do exactly that, each wrapping itself in
   `px-4 py-3`. This one wrapped itself in nothing, so both forms sat flush
   against the card's edges: the labels started a few pixels LEFT of the
   heading above them, and the segmented controls touched the right border.

   Matched to the clock beside it rather than to chrome.body() (`px-4 py-5`),
   so the four cards on this page have one rhythm. #}
<div class="px-4 py-3">

<form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_compose_behavior_update') }}" data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-compose-behavior') }}">

    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.forward_quote'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.forward_quote_hint'|trans }}</span>
        </span>

        <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
             role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.forward_quote'|trans }}">
            {% for folded in [true, false] %}
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="forwardQuoteCollapsed" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ folded ? '1' : '0' }}"
                           data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                           {{ forwardQuoteCollapsed == folded ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ (folded ? 'settings.compose_behavior.folded' : 'settings.compose_behavior.open')|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# Second question, its own form for the same reason the first one has one: each
   control submits on change, and a shared form would post both keys every time
   either moved. The controller only writes the key it is sent, so the two
   cannot overwrite each other. #}
<form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_compose_behavior_update') }}" class="mt-4" data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-compose-behavior') }}">

    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.send_feedback'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.send_feedback_hint'|trans }}</span>
        </span>

        <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
             role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.send_feedback'|trans }}">
            {% for option in ['optimistic', 'hold'] %}
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="sendFeedback" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ option }}"
                           data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                           {{ sendFeedback == option ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ ('settings.compose_behavior.send_' ~ option)|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# Third, and not a setting plMail stores: which program a mailto: link opens
   is the BROWSER's choice, per browser and per device, so there is nothing to
   post. The button asks the browser (settings--mailto-handler says what it can
   and cannot know about the answer). An installed plMail in Chromium offers
   itself through the manifest's protocol_handlers without this — and inside
   that app the button is swapped for the system's own steps (#587).

   The URL is the one ComposeController reads; `%s` is where the browser puts
   the whole link, and is appended rather than passed to path(), which would
   encode the percent sign into `%25s`. #}
<div class="mt-4 flex items-start justify-between gap-3"
     data-controller="settings--mailto-handler"
     data-settings--mailto-handler-url-value="{{ path('app_compose_new') }}?mailto=%s"
     data-settings--mailto-handler-labels-value="{{ {
         asked:       'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_asked'|trans,
         failed:      'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_failed'|trans,
         insecure:    'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_insecure'|trans,
         unsupported: 'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_unsupported'|trans,
         app_macos:   'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_app_macos'|trans,
         app_windows: 'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_app_windows'|trans,
         app_linux:   'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_app_linux'|trans,
         app_other:   'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_app_other'|trans,
     }|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}">
    <span class="min-w-0">
        <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.mailto'|trans }}</span>
        <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_hint'|trans }}</span>
        <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink mt-1" data-settings--mailto-handler-target="state" role="status" hidden></span>
    </span>

    <button type="button"
            class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                   bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-accent-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer
                   disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-40"
            data-settings--mailto-handler-target="button"
            data-action="click->settings--mailto-handler#register">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-at text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {{ 'settings.compose_behavior.mailto_button'|trans }}
    </button>
</div>

</div>
